// Which creatures' and characters' animations the SPAN 2x upscale sharpens in its Balanced mode (Preferences, Mobile
// upscale; `world_rendering.mobile_upscale = "balanced"`), while the view magnifies the art 1.5 times or more. Off
// upscales none, and Always upscales every body whatever the cost, but those listed upscale="never" below: it reads
// neither the size rule nor the "always" entries. Dynamapper reads your copy, cache/runtime_specs/mobiles/Upscale.kdl beside the
// assets folder, in place of this file when it exists, at startup: copy this file there and edit the copy. A copy that
// does not read leaves this file in force, with a warning naming the line, until it is fixed.
//
// A body upscales whole or not at all: every action and direction at 2x, or all at 1x, so its sharpness does not
// change from one action to the next. A rider and its mount are each a body of their own.
//
//   default max_canvas=<side>
//     The size rule, for the bodies not listed: a body upscales when each of its animations (or, in a RIFE in-between
//     mode, each of its RIFE sequences, whose in-between cards hold two frames) fits a canvas of <side> by <side>
//     pixels or fewer, its frames with a 2-pixel border, rounded up to 8 per side. <side> is 8 to 260; without this
//     line, 260. At 260 the dragons, wyrms, daemons and great UOP bodies play at 1x: a larger body upscales in tiles,
//     several runs of the network per frame, and takes seconds to finish.
//
//   body <id> [<last id>] [package="cc"|"ec"] upscale="always"|"never"
//     The body of in-game id <id> (the server's, as a mobile's body is sent), or every id from <id> to <last id>:
//     "always" upscales it whatever its size (in tiles when large), "never" keeps it at 1x, in Always too. With
//     package, the entry holds for that package's animations only, "cc" the Classic ones and "ec" the Enhanced ones,
//     and comes before an entry without one. A body is listed once per package, and once without one.
//
// For example:
//   body 12 package="cc" upscale="always"   // the Classic dragon at 2x
//   body 400 401 upscale="never"            // human bodies at 1x in both packages, in Balanced and Always

default max_canvas=260
